Reason:
The fix introduces uacce_stop_queue as a separate function that only stops the queue if it is in the UACCE_Q_STARTED state, then transitions it to UACCE_Q_INIT. The UACCE_CMD_PUT_Q ioctl now only stops the queue without calling put_queue, deferring actual resource release to the final cleanup (uacce_put_queue) which is called only when the file descriptor is closed or device is removed. The new uacce_put_queue first calls uacce_stop_queue, then checks if the queue is in UACCE_Q_INIT state before calling ops->put_queue. This ensures ops is only accessed when the queue is in a valid state and after proper synchronization, preventing access to freed or NULL pointers during the race condition.


